// Title: Potential LSASS Process Dump Via Procdump
// Sigma ID: 5afee48e-67dd-4e03-a783-f74259dcf998
// Status: stable | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2018-10-30 | Modified: 2025-10-19
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1036, credential-access, T1003.001
// Tags: car.2013-05-009
// Description: Detects potential credential harvesting attempts through LSASS memory dumps using ProcDump. This
//   rule identifies suspicious command-line patterns that combine memory dump flags (-ma, -mm, -mp)
//   with LSASS-related process markers. LSASS (Local Security Authority Subsystem Service) contains
//   sensitive authentication data including plaintext passwords, NTLM hashes, and Kerberos tickets
//   in memory. Attackers commonly dump LSASS memory to extract credentials for lateral movement and
//   privilege escalation.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely, because no one should dump an lsass process memory
//   - Another tool that uses command line flags similar to ProcDump
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sysinternals/downloads/procdump
//   - https://research.splunk.com/endpoint/3742ebfe-64c2-11eb-ae93-0242ac130002
//   - https://x.com/wietze/status/1958302556033065292?s=12
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_sysinternals_procdump_lsass.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains " -ma " or ProcessCommandLine contains " /ma " or ProcessCommandLine contains " –ma " or ProcessCommandLine contains " —ma " or ProcessCommandLine contains " ―ma " or ProcessCommandLine contains " -mm " or ProcessCommandLine contains " /mm " or ProcessCommandLine contains " –mm " or ProcessCommandLine contains " —mm " or ProcessCommandLine contains " ―mm " or ProcessCommandLine contains " -mp " or ProcessCommandLine contains " /mp " or ProcessCommandLine contains " –mp " or ProcessCommandLine contains " —mp " or ProcessCommandLine contains " ―mp ") and (ProcessCommandLine contains " ls" or ProcessCommandLine contains " keyiso" or ProcessCommandLine contains " samss")
